No source code from any other project is included in this repository. The
library in src/ was written from the pseudocode fragments in fragments/, which
describe, in our own words, designs and measured results observed in the
projects below, and from public format specifications (GGUF block layouts,
safetensors, OCP Microscaling MX, IEEE/OCP FP8). Each fragment's "Origin:"
line records which project(s) it came from. The consensus scoring in
fragments/CONSENSUS.md counts how many independent projects converge on each
pattern.

Projects studied (tag, repository, licence at time of reading, Oct 2026):

  colibri        https://github.com/JustVugg/colibri              Apache-2.0
  ds4            https://github.com/antirez/ds4                   MIT
  pulsar         https://github.com/giannisanni/pulsar            MIT
  monolite       https://github.com/Pioshin/monolite              Apache-2.0
  slipstream     https://github.com/Schero94/slipstream           MIT
  ktransformers  https://github.com/kvcache-ai/ktransformers      Apache-2.0
  apus           https://github.com/bricesommers/apus-glm5.3-flash PolyForm-NC-1.0.0
  flashmoe       https://github.com/danveloper/flash-moe          no licence

Two of the studied projects are not open-source licensed for general use
(apus: PolyForm Noncommercial; flashmoe: no licence). They were read for
experimental research only. Fragments whose only origin is [apus] or
[flashmoe] are marked as such; review fragments/CONSENSUS.md before relying on
a pattern with a single non-commercial or unlicensed origin in a commercial
setting.

The expert-pruning criterion follows the published REAP method
(https://github.com/CerebrasResearch/reap, arXiv:2510.13999).

The decision-engine design (src/lib/tlm_decide.*) follows the publicly
described typed-question interface of the Jev family of decision models
(Choice, Score, Noul); no model weights or code from them are included.
